      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Tile based rendering on standalone isn't comparable to PCVR.\n\nYou can already add AudioLink to Mobile Toon Standard in SDK 3.10.5-beta.1 (unannounced).\n\nAudio sources are kinda expensive, voices take priority.\n\nQuest 2 is still supported with feature updates until December 2026, security updates until 2027. And VRChat on Android/iOS is still sticking to the 6 GB minimum RAM requirement, just like the Quest 2.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-08-31T01:41:27.531Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since VRChat always crash easily on the quest 2 only, why not make the quest 3/3s have better graphics, better avatar capabilities, and more close to like PC \n\nYou should be able to add audio link on avatar since the items have audiolink that's quest comparable already, why not do the same with the avatars, and have sound\n\nThe Quest 2 can bearly run VRChat without low memory issues,no avatars showing, less world capability, and it crash easily \n\nJust make the Quest 3/3s more optimized \n\nthank you",
